{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/313784-help-me-understand","id":313784,"title":"help me understand...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-16T09:39:33-08:00","id":313784,"title":"help me understand...","content":"I am probably going to start running demon soon, and need some help. <br /> <br /> In a lot of ways I understand demon, but in some i don't, specifically when dealing with the rest of the world of darkness.<br /> <br /> 1.) I understand the nature of the god machine is left intentionally vague, and that it talks about how the GM intentionally reared religious art and documents to incorporate itself, however; is the GM, god? If not can the two simultaneously exist? <br /> <br /> 2.) if the GM and god simultaneously exist, can GM demons, and infernal demons simultaneously exist? And if so how do they interact with one another? <br /> <br /> 3.) Is my understanding that in the context of demon the descent, hell is state of complete absence from the god machine, and not a misery filled fire plane? <br /> <br /> 4.) do the god machine angels have their own personalities, desires, or even personal goals, it suggests so in the book where it describes example angels, however, where does the lack of free will come into play? Do angels have free will all along, it's only when they act on it, do they fall? <br /> <br /> Thanks for any answers, i know that's a lot of questions. <br /> <br /> I'm hoping to make a fun and interesting game for my friends, and i want to start off on the right foot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1898-wadesauce","name":"wadesauce","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1898_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T09:57:54-08:00","id":313810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wadesauce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/313784-help-me-understand#post313784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am probably going to start running demon soon, and need some help.<br /> <br /> In a lot of ways I understand demon, but in some i don't, specifically when dealing with the rest of the world of darkness.<br /> <br /> 1.) I understand the nature of the god machine is left intentionally vague, and that it talks about how the GM intentionally reared religious art and documents to incorporate itself, however; is the GM, god? If not can the two simultaneously exist?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can if you want. The game doesn't confirm or deny the existence of an abrahamic god, it's entirely focused on the Machine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wadesauce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/313784-help-me-understand#post313784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2.) if the GM and god simultaneously exist, can GM demons, and infernal demons simultaneously exist? And if so how do they interact with one another?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing says they can't, and there is no guidelines on how they'd interact if they would at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wadesauce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/313784-help-me-understand#post313784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3.) Is my understanding that in the context of demon the descent, hell is state of complete absence from the god machine, and not a misery filled fire plane?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the Unchained, &quot;Hell&quot; is a philosophical idea which manifests in different ways for each Demon. It's a personal idea of paradise for them in a deliberate inversion of the usual abrahamic principle. This has no bearing on any other place people might conceivably label Hell, as it's an idea rather than a particular place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wadesauce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/313784-help-me-understand#post313784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4.) do the god machine angels have their own personalities, desires, or even personal goals, it suggests so in the book where it describes example angels, however, where does the lack of free will come into play? Do angels have free will all along, it's only when they act on it, do they fall?</div> </div> </div> </div>Angels are autonomous beings which act in the interest of the God-Machine, they <i>do </i>have personalities, but not really personal goals. They have their Mission, and that defines them. The moment they start thinking about other things or get distracted from their Mission, they inch closer to their Fall. They have free will in the sense that there isn't a hard constraint on their behavior thanks to the Machine, but unless they're in the process of Falling or are about to Fall, it's unlikely that they'll deviate from their mission. (They have wide latitude to decide how they're going to complete that mission.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T10:09:38-08:00","id":313830,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the response. World of darkness is a strange place, because it involves so many creation myths, and so many ancient mysteries. It's hinted that the abrahmic god and Satan exists through a lot of hunter and vampire sources, but then you have the primordial beginnings of werewolf the forsaken (my personal favorite creation myth.) and all the others.. I've not even looked at mummies, but i assume that shakes things up as well.. <br /> <br /> I'm asking all this so if I incorporated vampire, hunter, infernal or Devine beings, or whatever, that I'd do it in the most fluff friendly way possible,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1898-wadesauce","name":"wadesauce","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1898_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T11:25:50-08:00","id":313861,"title":"","content":"None of them are mutually exclusive, nor are they all encompassing.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, there has been absolutely no indication that either abrahamic god or satan exist.<br /> <br /> There's been a few different kinds of Angels which've been poorly detailed, and a bunch of different kinds of Demons that have been detailed. Ostensibly divine powers which always have their divinity called into question in the same space they're introduced, etc.<br /> <br /> You don't run the risk of breaking anything by having them all in there. You do run the risk of giving yourself a headache if you attempt to unify them all into one cosmology.<br /> <br /> It's beneficial to note that even in real world mythologies nothing is ever so clear and coherent as gamers seem to think thanks to our DnD influenced conception of metaphysics. If you understand that everything <i>isn't </i>necessarily connected, that's the best position to be in, IMO.<br /> <br /> Lastly, nWoD is intentionally toolboxy in its approach, which is also worth keeping in mind when you're reviewing secondary sourcebooks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T12:16:32-08:00","id":313886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wadesauce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/313784-help-me-understand?p=313830#post313830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the response. World of darkness is a strange place, because it involves so many creation myths, and so many ancient mysteries.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point is, there's only darkness and shadows. There's no truth. It's a world where things like the Unchained and acamoth and strix and maeltinet, etc. can coexist and can equally be called &quot;demons&quot;. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T12:46:57-08:00","id":313910,"title":"","content":"Yea there is not really a statement on whether YHVH exists in <b>Demon</b> or not.<br /> <br /> One thing to bear in mind from a sort of religious scholarship direction is the GM does seem similar to some accounts of a Demiurge, or physical opposite of God(s) spirtual being in Gnostic thought. In other words, something as physical and flawed as God/YHVH is spiritual and perfect. The Demiurge (which may or may not be a Satan stand in) often tries to ape the more perfect spiritual God. That...actually describes the God Machine pretty well. If you are looking to have both YHVH or some similar Abrahamaic God as well as the GM, that is a direction to take it. It also raises the interesting (to me) question of if the GM is the opposite of God/YHVH, that makes it's &quot;Angels&quot; essentially Demons...so what are Demons?<br /> <br /> However you use the WoD vision of God(s), the Principal, presented in <b>Promethean</b>, is anouther interesting wrinkle. The Principle seems to be the (a?) source of souls and passion...Prometheans do make souls as part of their alchemical journey. More intriguing, it has Angels (the Qashmallim) carrying out it's will. Qashmallim also seem to follow very specific missions, and similarly try to nudge things, much like God Machine Angels. Indeed, there are a goodly number of similarities, except Qashmallim, being more perfect, don't fall. There is no Satan in relation to the Principle (though the Principle is not a caring force so much as a creative one) though with it's dynamism, the stagnation of the God Machine can come close. The God Machine can make an excellent Demiurge to the Principle's more spiritual being. More on the Principle is in <b>Promethean: The Created</b> and <b>Pandora's Book</b>.<br /> <br /> I have the Principle as a metaphysically somewhat connected element to the God Machine in my Chronicle, though most Demons know little to nothing about it. There are a couple Qashmallim in my setting, though, that the PCs will eventually interact with and raise questions.<br /> <br /> Of course, if you want a more purely bibilical YHVH, the Principle just muddies the water, and does not bring any demons if you are looking for something out of Dante for rival Infernal Demons.<br /> <br /> There are the Vice Spirits from the Lower Depths detailed in Inferno, but they don't really have a divine opposite (much as the Principle lacks an infernal) but given the Principle is not tied to Virtue and the Vice Spirits don't really represent any sort of stagnation, they don't make good oppositional forces as they have nothing connecting them beyond similarity to Angels and Demons. I assume the GM would regard them as things that don't belong in relaity and work against them to some degree, but nothing more special then that unless you make it such. If you are looking for something biblical, the vice spirits of Inferno just, again, muddy the waters, but if you want rival demons they can work. More on these Demons is in <b>Inferno.</b><br /> <br /> There is also the Lucifuge, but there are more questions than answers as to their origin. They apparently have demonic heritage, but the specifics are kept vague. More on the Lucifuge is in <b>Hunter: The Vigil</b> and <b>Compacts and Conspiracies</b>.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T14:25:54-08:00","id":313973,"title":"","content":"If it's any help in my game demons and angels understood from a traditional point of view are powerful spirits associated with the virtues and vices of humanity. They are organized in hierarchies, each group has it's own spiritual realm and they take forms and names from humanity cultural heritage. However they are not &quot;true&quot; demons and angels, those are the servants of the god machine. As for interaction since they have different objectives they generally ignore each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T06:51:16-08:00","id":314430,"title":"","content":"It is really hard for me to not try and connect it all into a single cosmology. I understand everything is set up to be a big mystery, and a big toolbox for the story teller, but i have a completion ocd problem. Lol. <br /> <br /> Thank you for your responses","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1898-wadesauce","name":"wadesauce","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1898_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T09:53:40-08:00","id":314643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wadesauce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/313784-help-me-understand?p=314430#post314430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is really hard for me to not try and connect it all into a single cosmology. I understand everything is set up to be a big mystery, and a big toolbox for the story teller, but i have a completion ocd problem. Lol.<br /> <br /> Thank you for your responses</div> </div> </div> </div>When someone asks me how to &quot;perfectly connect all the dots&quot;, i usually use a quote from the marvels &quot;The Eternals&quot; 2006 series:<br /> <br /> &quot;There are things for which humans have no frame of reference. Have you ever tried to explain democracy to a bacteria? Try discussing the Holy Trinity with a blade of grass. There are things for which you [humans] have no frame of reference.&quot;<br /> <br /> (the quote is not literal, but it went more or less that way)<br /> <br /> It's like trying to explain a cube to someone who lives in a world where only lenght and width exist. You can only give him a glimpse of what a cube is... and a headache, which is an expression that always comes up when someone tries to explain the cosmology in nWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2213,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","user":"TittoPaolo210","date":". 11-17-2014, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2213-tittopaolo210","name":"TittoPaolo210","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T17:02:40-08:00","id":314940,"title":"","content":"I've got an example to bring up about the inter-connectivity issue that might be more practical from a ST's standpoint.<br /> <br /> Imagine if you will, a city that possesses a large population of both Kindred and Unchained. And in that hypothetical city both creatures have not once become aware of the other's nature for the last thousand years. From the Unchained's perspective they've run into strange creatures that, like themselves, masquerade as being ordinary humans but are incredibly long lived, again like themselves, and run off pure life energy that can only be process directly from the blood of humans and animals. There are of course legends and popular fables about vampires and the living dead, but unless one of the Demon's former mission was to eliminate or protect Kindred who somehow wound up as a part of Infrastructure then the average Demon wouldn't really be equipped with the proper knowledge about Vampires to correctly identify them as such. From the Demon's perspective the Vampires of the city would be more closely categorized as a Cryptid or just an ordinary human who was genetically altered by the God Machine for some purpose in the past. Just because the ST and the players are aware of what Vampires, Werewolves, Mages, and all the other strange things in heaven and earth are doesn't mean that the characters will have a single clue as to what's really going on. In the above example both the Vampire's and Demon's continued existence heavily depends upon the whole world at large recognizing them as just an ordinary human, and if role played correctly can add a rich layer of mystery to your world that keeps all of the players on edge.<br /> <br /> As for integrating (What has fallen may rise again) a Judeo-Christian theme into your chronicle the only advice I can give is some fantastic advice <b>shadowhowler</b> gave me regarding how to describing what a Mage sees when using Mage Sight: &quot;Tell them what they see, not what it is.&quot;<br /> <br /> I hope this is helpful and wish you luck on your Chronicle. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}